.TITLE "launchctl"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Manages `launchd`, the service management framework on macOS. This command-line
utility is used to load, unload, enable, and disable system-level daemons
and user-level agents. It provides fine-grained control over background
processes and scheduled tasks.

.DIV "ALIAS"
**services**

.DIV "TLDR"
**launchctl list**
Lists all loaded agents and daemons for the current user.
> 

**launchctl load __~/Library/LaunchAgents/my.agent.plist__**
Loads a user agent defined by the specified __.plist__ file.
> __~/Library/LaunchAgents/my.agent.plist__: The path to the LaunchAgent .plist file.

**launchctl unload __~/Library/LaunchAgents/my.agent.plist__**
Unloads a previously loaded user agent.
> __~/Library/LaunchAgents/my.agent.plist__: The path to the LaunchAgent .plist file.

**launchctl enable __system/com.apple.coreservicesd__**
Enables a system daemon, making it persistent across reboots.
> __system/com.apple.coreservicesd__: The service identifier.

**launchctl disable __user/501/com.apple.Spotlight__**
Disables a user agent, preventing it from loading automatically.
> __user/501/com.apple.Spotlight__: The service identifier for user 501.

.DIV "SUMMARY"
`launchctl` is a powerful and complex tool. Misconfiguring `launchd` items
can lead to system instability. Always consult the `launchd.plist` man page
for details on creating and managing property list files.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:defaults**

